# Hooks reference

What runs automatically in this repo, where it is wired, and how it is tested. Claude Code hook docs: https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks

## How hooks work here

- A hook is a command that fires on an event (`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SessionStart`, ...). Each entry has a `matcher` (a regex over the tool name) and a command. The payload arrives on stdin as JSON and includes the session's `cwd`.
- `PreToolUse` hooks can block: exit 2 blocks the call and feeds stderr back to Claude. Exit 1 does not block, so every guard exits 2 on any failure.
- **Fail closed.** The guards block on a bad payload, an unknown profile, a broken profile file or a crash.
- **Worktrees.** In a worktree session, settings, agents, commands and hook scripts load from the main checkout, and `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` points there. Hooks that resolve file paths use the payload `cwd` (the worktree) through `.claude/hooks/repo-root.mjs`. A guard change made on a branch is live only after it merges and main is pulled, which is why the main checkout stays on `main` (`AGENTS.md` "Git & PRs").
- Persona guards run only when that persona runs as a sub-agent. Slash commands and the main session use the session's own permissions.

## Session hooks (`.claude/settings.json`)

| Event | Matcher | Command | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Stop` | (all) | `echo` | Reminds you to consider `/retro`. |

The same file holds `permissions.deny` for Read and Edit on `.env` files at any depth (E5, `.agents/rules/env-and-secrets.md`) and the `permissions.allow` list described in `.agents/rules/commands.md`.

## Persona guards (`.claude/agents/*.md` frontmatter)

| Guard | Used by | What it allows |
|---|---|---|
| `bash-guard.mjs read-only` | reviewer, retro | Git inspection (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`, `ls-files`, `merge-base`, `rev-parse`, `branch --show-current`) and the exact check commands |
<!-- kit:if has.db -->
| `bash-guard.mjs architect` | architect | The read-only commands, plus the exact local-database commands |
| `path-guard.mjs <paths>` | architect (`{{DB_PATH}}`, `.agents/memory/decisions.md`), retro (`.agents/memory/lessons.md`, `docs/next-steps.md`) | Edit and Write (retro has only Edit) only inside the listed paths, resolved against the session's checkout |
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !has.db -->
| `bash-guard.mjs architect` | architect | The read-only commands |
| `path-guard.mjs <paths>` | architect (`.agents/memory/decisions.md`), retro (`.agents/memory/lessons.md`, `docs/next-steps.md`) | Edit and Write (retro has only Edit) only inside the listed paths, resolved against the session's checkout |
<!-- kit:end -->

The profiles live in `.claude/hooks/guard-profiles.mjs`, which is the source of truth; this table is a summary. harness-kit generated them from this repo's commands; edit that file to change them. Commands match exactly, so `<test command> some-file` is blocked unless that exact line is listed. Every profile also rejects shell metacharacters (separators, pipes, redirects, quotes, `$`, backslashes), inline env assignments and git's `--output`; only `&&` chaining is allowed. The planner and researcher have no Bash tool at all.
<!-- kit:if module.prePush -->

## Git hook (`.githooks/pre-push`)

Refuses pushes to `main`. Arm it once per clone with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (worktrees share it). Only {{OWNER}} uses the `{{ENV_PREFIX}}_ALLOW_PUSH_MAIN=1` override, and nobody uses `--no-verify`.
<!-- kit:end -->

## Tests

`{{CMD_HOOK_TESTS}}` runs the hook tests (`.claude/hooks/guards.test.mjs` and any skill-script or git-hook tests). Run it after any guard, hook or skill-script change. The bash-guard cases are derived from `guard-profiles.mjs`; add a case to `guards.test.mjs` for any pattern you write by hand.

## Adding a hook

- Add one only after skipping the manual step has bitten us at least once. Hooks should make the right thing the easy thing.
- Keep hooks fast, because they run on every matching tool call, and never auto-run tests on every edit.
- A new guard fails closed and gets tests in the same PR.

